# Ship finished work to Vercel

When you finish product, UI, feature, or bugfix work on this campus site, **commit (if there are changes) and `git push origin main`** so Vercel deploys to https://campus.assetpilotedu.com.

Do **not** wait for the user to say “push to Vercel” unless they said not to ship yet (e.g. “don’t deploy”, “hold the push”, “local only”).

## Git safety (always)

- Never update git config
- Never force push, `--no-verify`, amend (unless the user’s commit rules allow it), or `git -i`
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets
- If a hook fails, create a **new** commit — do not amend

## How

1. `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -8` in parallel
2. Stage only the product files you changed (plus this rule if you edited it)
3. Commit with a why-focused message (PowerShell here-string on Windows)
4. `git push origin main` and confirm the production URL
